@node Usage
@chapter Usage
@code{wg-vpn homeLAN full} and @code{wg-vpn workLAB full} install the guard before activating their NetworkManager profiles.
@code{wg-vpn homeLAN split} and @code{wg-vpn workLAB split} leave ordinary Internet access via the physical connection.
@code{wg-vpn homeLAN stop} disconnects the guarded full VPN and removes its protection intentionally.
@code{wg-vpn status}, @code{wg-vpn --help}, and @code{wg-vpn gui} provide diagnostics and controls.
@node Security
@chapter Security and limitations
The green guest LED means direct Internet routing is permitted. Physical interfaces still carry encrypted VPN transport and allowed LAN traffic when the guest LED is off.
Always activate full tunnels through @code{wg-vpn}; direct NetworkManager activation bypasses pre-arming.
IPv6 leakage protection, changing network interfaces, DNS re-resolution, and incoming SSH must be tested on the deployment system.
Do not include real VPN keys, DNS endpoints or private IP addresses in a public repository.
@bye
